  ran: true
  outcome: "Checklist walked row by row. 'Behaviour changed or got defined?' — no: this WU ships no code and UC-5's contract is untouched. 'Non-obvious choice made or reversed?' — YES, and examined rather than assumed: this run reversed leg selection from BodyViewer to the panel, which deletes a shipped control and redirects W7 and W8. Judged SCREEN-LOCAL and deliberately not written to docs/decisions/: the reversal is recorded in the run's Tune 8, in its blocked-on, and now in the epic plan's W7/W8 rows, which is where a reader of W7 actually meets it. If a third screen needs the same leg-scoping rule, that second sighting is the signal to open a DEC and the design-rules entry with it. 'Design convention surfaced or locked?' — not yet, by the same reasoning: one sighting is not a pattern. 'Component map or invariant changed?' — no. 'Repeating process changed?' — no. 'T0 rule?' — no. NOTE: an earlier version of this note cited DEC-16 to conclude 'nothing to distil UP'. That was a misread — DEC-16 governs a built component's design file retiring into its TSDoc, and has no bearing on a screen run — and it let the 'reversed choice' row go unexamined behind the wrong rule. Found at the Tier-3 review; the row is examined above on its own terms."
